  "description": "Repairs r-def-cat-txn/cat-drop-table-held-recordset: the catalog helper read a cached TableDefs collection, so T still showed after the second DROP TABLE returned no error; there was no independent post-state read. In a new ACCDB with T (3 rows): a dynaset on T is opened and positioned; DROP TABLE T is executed (DBEngine.Errors right after); the refreshed TableDefs are listed; the held recordset's RecordCount, MoveNext and row are read and it is closed; DROP TABLE T is executed again (DBEngine.Errors before and after), the refreshed TableDefs are listed and SELECT * FROM T is run. The Database is closed and reopened read-only and the refreshed TableDefs are listed and SELECT * FROM T is run again.",
